BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Moneymeds) Tj T* () Tj T* (Moneymeds: Executive Summary) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Many young adults with chronic conditions have to make difficult choices about their) Tj T* (medication. Aging off a parent's insurance plan, working part-time or gig jobs, or enrolling in) Tj T* (a high-deductible plan often leaves them paying a large share of prescription costs themselves.) Tj T* (Surveys of patients regularly report that a meaningful portion of people skip doses, split) Tj T* (pills or delay refills because of cost. For someone managing asthma, diabetes or a mental) Tj T* (health condition, these choices can lead to emergency visits that cost far more than the) Tj T* (medication would have.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The tools that could help are fragmented. The cash price of one prescription can differ a great) Tj T* (deal from one pharmacy to the next, even within a single neighborhood. Discount cards,) Tj T* (manufacturer savings coupons, patient assistance programs and pharmacy loyalty programs each) Tj T* (have their own rules, and no single place tells a patient which one to use. Young adults in) Tj T* (particular are often new to managing their own health costs and have had little guidance on how) Tj T* (to do it.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Moneymeds is a mobile app that does three things in one place. First, it compares prescription) Tj T* (prices across nearby pharmacies based on the user's medications and location. Second, it) Tj T* (identifies which discount program or coupon applies and shows the resulting price, so the user) Tj T* (does not have to test several cards at the counter. Third, it offers a simple monthly health) Tj T* (budget that accounts for refills, copays, deductibles and upcoming appointments, and sends) Tj T* (reminders before a refill is due so users can shop around ahead of time.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The app is designed for people who are not experts in healthcare. We use plain language, short) Tj T* (onboarding and a focus on the few decisions that matter most: where to fill a prescription,) Tj T* (which program to use and how much to set aside each month. We also include short educational) Tj T* (content explaining terms such as deductible, formulary and generic substitution, since many of) Tj T* (our target users have never had to learn them.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our target customers are U.S. adults ages 18 to 34 with at least one chronic condition) Tj T* (requiring ongoing prescription medication. Public health data suggests that a substantial share) Tj T* (of young adults live with a chronic condition, and a large portion of them report some) Tj T* (difficulty affording care. We estimate that several million people fall in this group) Tj T* (nationally, though we have not yet refined this figure. Our initial focus is students and) Tj T* (recent graduates in the region around our university, where we can reach users through campus) Tj T* (health centers, student groups and local clinics.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Beyond individual consumers, we see secondary markets in campus health services, employers who) Tj T* (want to support younger employees, and community clinics that help patients find affordable) Tj T* (medication. We have not yet tested interest in any of these.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (We plan to earn revenue in two ways. The first is referral fees paid by discount program) Tj T* (providers and pharmacies when a user fills a prescription through a Moneymeds recommendation.) Tj T* (The second is a premium subscription of a few dollars per month offering features such as) Tj T* (family sharing, expanded budgeting tools and refill planning across multiple medications. The) Tj T* (core price comparison would remain free so that cost is never a barrier for the users we most) Tj T* (want to reach.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We recognize that referral revenue depends on agreements we have not yet signed, and that) Tj ET
